title: mf duplicate keep
tags: [[CLI command]] Duplicates
kind: reference
summary: Keep the copies a query matches: trash their twins outside it

In every group with a copy matching the query, every copy that does not match goes
to the trash; a group with no copy matching it is left alone. The copies to trash
are themselves a query, `same(mfr_duplicate_group, Q) AND NOT Q`, and each has a twin
in `Q` that the run leaves, so no group loses its last copy
([[Deleting duplicate copies]]).

```
mf duplicate keep 'mfr_path ->* "/photos/sorted"'
mf duplicate keep -s 'keep=true'
```

It lists the paths, the number of groups and the space the trash will reclaim once
pruned, then asks (`-y` skips the question); `--dry-run` stops after the list. A
failure stops the run, saying how many copies were already trashed: they have left
their groups, and running it again plans afresh from what remains.
